# UPDATE (2026-08-21): moved to tlcs900_backend@970c4a75312e, a new commit ON
# TOP of 2a221caa88dd as the immutability policy requires. That commit makes the
# memory-operand forms reachable under their real mnemonics -- `and (xix), 0x7f`
# instead of only `andmi8 (xix), 0x7f` -- and keeps every old spelling as an
# InstAlias, because this tree uses them in hundreds of files (bitm in 53
# sources, incm in 80). Both spellings emit identical encodings.
#
# Why it matters here: the tree must assemble byte-exactly, so a byte run could
# only become an instruction if llvm-mc accepted it. It did not accept the forms
# that make up large stretches of v7 still carried as .byte -- see
# scripts/analysis/llvm_missing_instruction_forms.py and docs/IS-IT-DONE.md.
#
# Verified with a full `make clean-all && make all` on this pin: 9/9 targets at
# 100.00% -- maincpu v7/v9/v10, subcpu payload v142, subcpu v142 update image,
